※ pl4g-test: compile=error
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4626 LANG_ELEMENT_REPLACED

※ At the top of a turn an array holds what a later line of the body put in it on the turn before:
※ here an element of the heap's, which the replacement on this turn gives back.  So what was read
※ at the top is dead after the replacement, though nothing of the heap's was in the array before
※ the loop began.

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    let v: mut str⟦1⟧ = ⟦"a"⟧
    let n: mut u8 = 0u8
    while n < 2u8:
        let x: str = v⟦0⟧
        v⟦0⟧ ← "b" ⧺ "c"
        if x = "bc":
            n ← n + 1u8
        n ← n + 1u8
    0u6
